    <bpmn:process id="W_W4652" name="W4652. Domestic Freight, Handling &amp; Inbound Cost Allocation to SKU" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Domestic inbound freight; DC handling; monthly allocation run
Frequency: Monthly
Volume: ~72,000 inbound receipts/yr; DC handling across 4 DCs
Owner: Cost Accounting Manager
Participants: Logistics (VS-06), DC Ops (VS-04), Freight (VS-110), AP (VS-15)
Source: workflow W4652 — Domestic Freight, Handling &amp; Inbound Cost Allocation to SKU</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4652_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4652_Lane1" name="Cost Accounting">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4652_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4652_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4652_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4652_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4652_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4652_Start3" name="Domestic inbound freight; DC handling; monthly allocation run">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4652_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4652_Task4" name="Allocate domestic inbound freight (line-haul DC-bound, DSD), DC…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Allocate domestic inbound freight (line-haul DC-bound, DSD), DC handling/receiving cost, and transfer freight (DC→store) to SKUs by an appropriate basis (weight, cube, case, value) per category policy; decide absorb-vs-billback posture (W4662)
Responsible (R): Cost Accounting / Logistics
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4652_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4652_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4652_Task5" name="Match freight/handling invoices to the receipts/shipments; post the cost to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Match freight/handling invoices to the receipts/shipments; post the cost to inventory or expense per the absorption policy; handle shared-shipment allocation across multiple SKUs/orders
Responsible (R): Cost Accounting / AP / Logistics
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4652_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4652_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
